The prebuilt gpt-live-host audio helper includes third-party software, each under its
own license. The main components:

  webrtc, rtc (webrtc-rs)   MIT OR Apache-2.0   https://github.com/webrtc-rs/webrtc
  cpal                      Apache-2.0          https://github.com/RustAudio/cpal
  sonora                    BSD-3-Clause        https://crates.io/crates/sonora
                            (a Rust port of WebRTC audio processing)
  libopus (via opusic-sys)  BSD-3-Clause        https://opus-codec.org
  opus                      MIT OR Apache-2.0   https://crates.io/crates/opus
  rubato                    MIT OR Apache-2.0   https://github.com/HEnquist/rubato
  ring                      Apache-2.0 AND ISC  https://github.com/briansmith/ring
  tokio                     MIT                 https://tokio.rs

The complete list of Rust dependencies and versions is in native/Cargo.lock; run
`cargo tree --manifest-path native/Cargo.toml` to see how they fit together.

